    "durationMs": 142647,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built and validated:\n\n**Implementation** (built from scratch — the workspace was empty)\n- `app/` — FastAPI app: `routers/links.py` (all endpoints), `models.py` (SQLAlchemy 2 `Link` model), `schemas.py` (pydantic validation), `config.py` (reads `DATABASE_URL` from env, no hard-coded credentials), `codes.py` (unique random code generation).\n- `alembic/` — migration `0001` creating the `links` table (unique indexed `code`, `url` TEXT, `clicks`, `created_at`).\n- `start.sh` — runs `alembic upgrade head` then serves uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; dependencies are pinned in `requirements.txt` and not installed in the script.\n- `README.md` — startup and API docs.\n\n**Key behaviors verified live**\n- `POST /links` → 201 with `{\"code\", \"url\", \"clicks\": 0}`; submitted URL returned byte-for-byte unchanged (case, port, query, fragment preserved); custom codes 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`, duplicates → 409 with `error`.\n- `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with `Location` exactly the stored URL, clicks incremented atomically (`UPDATE ... clicks + 1 RETURNING url`) exactly once per request.\n- `GET /links` → ascending creation order with `total`; `GET /links/{code}` → 200/404 with `error`.\n- All 422 paths (malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, invalid code) return an `error` field via custom exception handlers. I hardened URL validation beyond pydantic defaults: pydantic silently accepts `http:///no-host`, so the validator also requires a non-empty authority via `urlsplit`.\n- **Persistence**: restarted the server via `sh start.sh` and confirmed links and click counts survived.\n\n**Testing**: 10-test pytest suite (all passing), full curl smoke test of every endpoint, and idempotent re-run of migrations. Test rows were truncated afterward, so the database is clean for the automated suite."
